From 48c0456538be1c1a43d2873c1554afe044ae9f49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:58:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(grid): virtualized result grid with selection, copy
 and cell viewer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In-house data grid for query results (F-060 to F-064), on the M1-3 query
contract:

- DataGrid over a small RowSource interface (blocks of loaded rows,
  request, read, fullValue) so the table editor (M2-3) can reuse it;
  ResultGrid ({ resultId, summary }) feeds it a backend result through a
  bounded window cache (500-row windows, LRU by cells, nearest-first
  fetching, two requests at most, throttled while the viewport moves,
  refetch of the filling window while a result streams).
- Rows and columns virtualized; the rows area is drawn imperatively with
  recycled row and cell elements (no React render per scroll frame);
  sticky header and row-number layer; heights past 15M px are scaled.
- Typed rendering: numbers right-aligned in the monospace font, NULL,
  empty string and leading/trailing whitespace drawn distinctly, arrays as
  plain JSON, binary as 0x…, cut-cell marker, shimmer for rows loading.
- Columns: initial widths by kind, then fitted to the first rows; drag to
  resize, double-click to fit, drag to reorder.
- Selection of cells, ranges, rows, columns, all (mouse drag, shift and
  mod clicks, arrows, Page keys, Home/End, Mod+A, Shift/Mod+Space), focus
  ring, ARIA grid with aria-rowcount / aria-rowindex under virtualization.
- Copy: Mod+C (TSV), context menu "Copy as" TSV, CSV, JSON, Markdown,
  SQL INSERT, IN list, with or without headers; pure formatters, lossless
  numbers; rows not loaded and cut cells are read, bounded to 100 000 rows
  with a progress toast and a limit message.
- Cell viewer panel: whole value, JSON (exact numbers) and XML foldable,
  binary as a hex dump, copy, save (src/ipc/saveFile.ts; browser download
  in mock mode, disabled in the app until the backend can write a file).
- Footer: row count, streaming state, Load more / Load all.
- Dev page #grid (mock or real backend) and `pnpm perf:grid` (P-04).

Decisions: resultId is a number (the contract's type); TSV writes NULL
and '' as empty cells while CSV keeps them apart (empty vs ""); SQL
copies use ANSI identifier quoting and a `table_name` placeholder unless
the caller passes the dialect's quoting and a table; the row numbers are
a visual layer (rows carry aria-rowindex). No dependency added.

Task: M1-5

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
